Z||000000||Voyd||11-25-1999||11:55 PM||||whats the diffrence between a 85 SE and 85 GT in the interior or mechanicals?<P>i know the body is diffrent tho. i have a 85 SE but it has a GT front and maybe a GT back bumper, but not sure. are they even diffrent?<P>anyways, thanks for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-26-1999||12:13 AM||||According to Fiero by Gary Witzenberg the SE came with the 4 cyl but had the V6 as an option. Since the Ampmeter didn't exist and the oil preasure was still on the tach in 85 the SE and GT interior were almost identical. The gauges were different. If you went with the V6 on the SE you got the 4 spd. If you stayed standard and got the 4 cyl you would get a 5 speed. This remained in effect until late 86 when the GT fast back finally got the Getrag/Muncie 5 speed.<P>Externally the GT got the front and rear facias different as well as lower body cladding.<P>I hope thats the right answer.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-26-1999||09:31 AM||||I have a 85 GT and a 85 SE. I did not notice any difference in gauges. What am I overlooking? Now the instrument faces are slightly changed (cleaned up) on my 87 SE, but both 85's look the same.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||11-26-1999||10:48 AM||||If the 85 is an SE with a 4 cylinder (it was standard) then the very least it would have a different tach. 4 cyls don't have a 6 grand redline. They both had the 85 mph speedo.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||11-26-1999||11:57 AM||||Ok, I forgot about the tach thing, I'd heard of that before, once. My 85 SE was originally a V6 (2M6), so that's why I didn't notice any difference in the gauges between the GT and SE.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Voyd||11-26-1999||12:49 PM||||my SE is a V6. thanks for the info WKDFIRO.<p>[This message has been edited by Voyd (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||7
Z||000006||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||09:21 PM||||What's the difference between an '85 GT and an '86 SE.  I have a chance to buy either of them for about the same amount of money, but I can't afford to buy both.  I haven't seen the GT yet, but know that it's an auto, pw, remote trunk rel., bad motor.  The SE has the extra gauges, stick and worn out but running motor, same options.||||reg||5
Z||000007||Terrybogin||11-26-1999||09:34 PM||||An 85 GT and a 86 SE will look pretty much identical. In 86, when the GT got the fastback style body, the SE picked up the aero package like the 85 GT had. One difference will be that the 86 has smooth body mouldings and the 85 has the grooved.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||11:55 PM||||The '86SE I'm looking at has the grooved mouldings.  It looks identical to an '85 GT except that the sail panels say "SE".  Which car should I buy?||||reg||5
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||11-27-1999||03:03 AM||||The option comes down to do you like stick or automatic? Do you want the tach that starts at the 4 O'clock position and the extra gauges? Oh, and do you want a third brake light, the 86 will have it. If the engine is worn out on the 86 do you think the clutch is far behind? Sounds like you are rebuilding an engine eventually either way eventually. Tough choice.<BR>Also I think that Terry meant the 86 GT had smooth moldings and the SE had the grooves. My boss has the 86 SE and it has the grooves. He liked it because it makes the door handle more integrated.||||reg||1
